WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.533 --> 00:00:05.633
A live shell in the beir-replication repo

2
00:00:06.233 --> 00:00:08.733
Source, the paper's published numbers, and committed run artifacts

3
00:00:09.333 --> 00:00:13.633
The claim: can a 2021 retrieval benchmark be reproduced on a laptop?

4
00:00:14.233 --> 00:00:15.933
Running BM25 on SciFact for real

5
00:00:16.333 --> 00:00:20.533
0.677 against a published 0.665, over 5,183 documents

6
00:00:21.233 --> 00:00:25.533
The first full sweep. TAS-B lands exactly. DPR misses by 0.058

7
00:00:26.233 --> 00:00:29.633
The clue: searching title_only scores 0.261

8
00:00:30.033 --> 00:00:33.533
Title plus the full text scores 0.260. The body is being discarded

9
00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:38.533
The cause: the context encoder truncates every document at 100 tokens

10
00:00:39.233 --> 00:00:43.533
Raise the limit and it climbs to 0.318 at 512 tokens

11
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:47.033
Every published cell reproduced. DPR now exact at 0.318

12
00:00:47.433 --> 00:00:50.133
Both tables are committed artifacts of a 12 minute run. The BM25 figure above ran live
